    'about.title': 'About', 'about.body': '<p><b>AbandonedWell Energy AI</b> – screening tool for shut-in and end-of-life oil & gas wells to be repurposed as closed-loop coaxial heat-exchanger wells.</p><ol><li><b>Data normalisation:</b> LAS/CSV import, BHT correction (Horner or Harrison 1983), gradient from temperature logs.</li><li><b>Temperature–depth model</b> with a P10–P90 range (Monte Carlo).</li><li><b>Heat-recovery simulation</b> after Ramey (1962).</li><li><b>Economics & risk:</b> NPV, LCOH, integrity and distance scores.</li></ol><p class="muted">Faculty of Petroleum – PetroVietnam University, 2026. Model v0.1 is not validated against field data; for screening only.</p>',
    'help.title': 'Data Formats', 'help.body': '<h4>LAS files (2.0 / 1.2)</h4><ul><li>The first curve is depth (DEPT); ft is converted to m.</li><li>Temperature logs (TEMP, MTEMP, BHT…) → gradient by linear regression.</li><li>BHT in ~Parameter (BHT, BHTEMP) → Harrison correction.</li><li>Multiple files can be selected; files with the same well name are merged.</li></ul><h4>Well-list CSV</h4><pre>id,name,location,depth_m,gradient_c100m,bht_c,bht1_c,dt1_h,bht2_c,dt2_h,tc_h,integrity,distance_km\nA-01,Well A-01,offshore,4200,3.4,,,,,,,good,0.5\nD-01,Well D-01,onshore,3200,,,112,6,121,12,4,good,4</pre><p>location: onshore | offshore · integrity: good | fair | poor</p>',
