    'dec.psiTitle': 'Formula of the well repurposing index Ψ',
    'dec.psiBody': '<p><b>Ψ = [ a·V + C·(1 − ρ<sup>L</sup>) ] ÷ [ I + a·O ]</b></p><p>a = (1 − (1+r)<sup>−L</sup>)/r · ρ = (1+g)/(1+r)</p><p>V: yearly revenue · O: yearly running cost · I: capital · C: P&amp;A cost today · g: P&amp;A cost escalation · r: discount rate · L: project life.</p><p>The numerator is everything gained (energy sold + P&amp;A pushed to the end of the project); the denominator is everything spent. <b>Ψ &gt; 1 ⇔ re-use beats plugging now.</b> Against deferral for n years, replace C·(1 − ρ<sup>L</sup>) by C·(ρ<sup>n</sup> − ρ<sup>L</sup>) + H·a<sub>n</sub>.</p><p>For an open-loop well selling heat, V follows directly from field data: Q = min( ṁ·c·ΔT , R<sub>f</sub>·A·h·(ρc)·ΔT / t<sub>L</sub> , D ), V = Q·τ·p, with ΔT = T<sub>seabed</sub> + G·(z − z<sub>water</sub>) − T<sub>inj</sub>.</p><p>Colours: green = beats both plugging now and deferral; amber = beats plugging now only; red = worse than plugging now.</p>', 'dec.plan': 'Field plan', 'dec.planQ': 'Heat allotted (kWth)', 'dec.planGain': 'Gain under the field plan', 'dec.evpi': 'Worth measuring (bn VND)',
